Subject: [PATCH] ath12k: balance the start reference on hash failure

Return the group start reference before unwinding REO/HIF/WMI. The failed
hash initializer owns its local allocation and must not be destroyed here.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -1051,6 +1051,7 @@
 	ret = ath12k_link_sta_rhash_tbl_init(ab);
 	if (ret) {
 		ath12k_warn(ab, "failed to init peer addr rhash table %d\n", ret);
+		ath12k_core_to_group_ref_put(ab);
 		goto err_reo_cleanup;
 	}
 
